{"ld": 720, "paper": "HP459", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Protect Federal Home Loan Banks That Lend Money to Insurer Members That Become Delinquent", "sponsor_id": "h-foley-robert", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bailey-donna", "h-flynn-paul", "s-haggan-david", "h-morris-joshua", "h-olsen-rolf"], "committee_code": "HCIFS", "committee_name": "Health Coverage, Insurance and Financial Services", "summary": {"text": "This bill protects federal home loan banks that lend money to an insurer and the insurer enters into a receivership, including:\n\n1. Limiting to no more than 10 days restraining, enjoining or otherwise preventing a person from enforcing the person's rights or cause of action under any pledge, security, credit, loan or other similar arrangement to which the federal home loan bank is a party; 2. Requiring the federal home loan bank to repurchase any excess federal home loan bank capital stock held by an insurer within 7 days of receiving a redemption request from the insurer, subject to certain conditions; 3. Requiring the federal home loan bank within 10 days of the appointment of a receiver to provide the Superintendent of Insurance a process and timeline to release certain collateral held by the federal home loan bank, payment of certain fees owed by the insurer and redeem or repurchase any excess federal home loan bank stock held by an insurer; 4. Requiring the federal home loan bank to provide to the superintendent any available options to renew or restructure the insurer's loan; and 5. Preventing the avoidance of any transfer of property or preference arising under or in connection to any pledge, security, credit, collateral, loan or other similar arrangement to which the federal home loan bank is a party, except for transfers made with actual intent to hinder, delay or defraud.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0459&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "